---
description: Enabled buttons and editable fields must not use gray styling
alwaysApply: true
---

# Enabled controls are not gray

Do **not** use gray / muted / chrome-idle fills or muted text for:

- Enabled buttons (not `:disabled` / `.is-busy` / `.is-disabled`)
- Enabled inputs, selects, and textareas that are **not** `readonly` / `:read-only` / `:disabled`

Those controls MUST use normal interactive colors (`--surface` or accent primary, `--text`, `--border` / `--accent` as appropriate) so they read as editable and clickable.

Gray / muted / mixed-bg styling is reserved for **disabled** or **readonly** controls only (so operators can tell they cannot edit).

```css
/* BAD — enabled control looks disabled */
button:not(:disabled) { background: var(--chrome-idle); color: var(--muted); }
input:not(:disabled):not(:read-only) { background: color-mix(... var(--muted) ...); }

/* GOOD — enabled vs readonly */
button:not(:disabled) { background: var(--surface); color: var(--text); }
input:read-only, input:disabled { background: color-mix(...); color: var(--muted); }
```
